-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/a863a472-2b24-5beb-a7a9-046a1abd390f
-- title:
--   Supersingular chart, valuation ring and q+1 nodes over a level field
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and for a natural number $N$ the field `modularFunctionFieldFull N` is the subfield of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the series $q$-expanded $j$-invariants $\mathrm{qExpand}_d\, j_q$ for the divisors $d \mid N$, while `modularFunctionFieldBar N` is the subfield of $\bar{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise images of those elements. The ambient field is `fieldBar q M'`, the subfield of $\bar{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise images of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, where $H =$ `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the group of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$.
--
--   **Data and hypotheses on the curve.** A prime $q$ with $5 \le q$; a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; a valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, that is, $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$, with `hW` saying that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places, namely those places $w$ that are rational (the structure map to the residue field of $w$ is surjective), are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(j) \in$ `ssJSet q`; the hypothesis `hle` that `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is contained in `fieldBar q M'`; a constant reduction datum $R_0$ of type `ConstantReduction A ↥(modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M')`, consisting of a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lying over $A$, a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` from it onto `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal and which is compatible with the residue map of $A$, together with a degree-preserving map on places compatible with divisors of elements of non-zero residue; the hypothesis `hR₀` that $R_0$ computes coefficientwise reduction, i.e. for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}((q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, viewed as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; and a chosen element $s$ of $W$, i.e. a supersingular place.
--
--   **Small constants.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and an element $\pi_0$ of $k_0$ lying in $A$, such that $A \cap k_0$ (formally, the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \bar{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is a henselian local ring (`hhens`), and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); and the hypothesis `hκ` that $A = (A \cap k_0) + \mathfrak m_A$, i.e. every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c \in k_0 \cap A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary prime and roots of unity.** A prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0$ of $k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$; and an element $\varpi_t$ of $k_0$ lying in $A$ such that $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **Base layer.** An intermediate field $K_b$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$ (so $K_b = k_0$), a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ with $x \in A_b$ if and only if $x \in A$ (`hAb`), and an element $\varpi_b \ne 0$ of $A_b$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   The field `fieldBar q M'` is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \hookrightarrow \bar{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ which is characterised by its coefficients, in the sense that $f \in F_0$ holds if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$ (as a series over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$) is the image of an element of $k_0$, there exists a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that the following hold.
--
--   (1) For $x \in k_0$: $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$; thus $W_0 \cap k_0 = A \cap k_0$.
--
--   (2) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (3) The image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (4) ($W_0$ lies over $s$.) For every $g \in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers`, such that $g$ has non-negative order at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ at which $j_q$ has non-negative order, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$: the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$, the resulting element of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ whose residue in the residue field of $A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of the image of $g$ and of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (5) ($W_0$ is level-stable.) For every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma \in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every $f \in F_0$ such that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` also lies in $F_0$: $f \in W_0$ if and only if `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in W_0$. Here `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` selected by the $q$-expansion condition `IsLevelAutBar` attached to $\zeta$ and $\gamma$, the identity if no such automorphism exists.
--
--   (6) (Affine chart.) There exist a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that:
--
--   (a) the structure map is the inclusion: for $a \in A_b$, the image of $a$ in $B$ is the image of $a$ under $\bar{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`;
--
--   (b) $B$ is contained in the compositum $k_0(K_b) \sqcup F_0$, the join of the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$ with $F_0$;
--
--   (c) that compositum is the fraction field of $B$: every element of it is of the form $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h \ne 0$;
--
--   (d) $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$;
--
--   (e) $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$;
--
--   (f) every $f \in B$ lies in $F_0$ and the resulting element of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$;
--
--   (g) the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is prime;
--
--   (h) $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\varpi_b$: an element $f$ of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ if and only if $f\,h = g$ for some $g, h \in B$ with $\varpi_b \nmid h$ in $B$;
--
--   (i) the image of $j_q$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $B$;
--
--   (j) $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$;
--
--   (k) (Drinfeld special fibre.) For every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $\kappa$ of $A$, every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field inside the Drinfeld function field, the fraction field of `CoordRing q κ`, of the subgroup generated by the actions `hFunctionFieldAction` of the elements $(1,\zeta')$ for $\zeta' \in C_s$) such that: the cardinality of $C_s$ is $2\cdot$`placeWidthChar q M' s`; the kernel of $\rho$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ agrees on $A_b$ with the reduction map, i.e. $\rho$ of the image of $a \in A_b$ is the image of the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; every element $z$ of `quotField` satisfies $z\,\rho(h) = \rho(g)$ for some $g, h \in B$ with $\rho(h) \ne 0$; $z$ lies in the range of $\rho$ if and only if $z$, viewed in the Drinfeld function field, lies in the image of `CoordRing q κ`; and the equivariance: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ such that the pair (`redQ q γ`, $1$) lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), and $f \in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹ f` $\in B$, the image under $\rho$ of `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹ f` equals the action of that pair through `hFunctionFieldAction` on $\rho(f)$;
--
--   (l) (The $q+1$ nodes.) There exists a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$ with the following properties. Its cardinality is $q+1$. For every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $O \in$ `nodes` there is $O' \in$ `nodes` such that for all $f \in F_0$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in F_0$ one has $f \in O$ if and only if `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in O'$; conversely, for every $\zeta$ and all $O, O' \in$ `nodes` there is $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with the same equivalence, so that the level action is transitive on `nodes`. Distinct $O, O' \in$ `nodes` are separated: there is $f \in F_0$ lying in both which is not a unit of $O$ but is a unit of $O'$. Furthermore, for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ satisfying $V \cap k_0 = A \cap k_0$ and the specialisation property of (4) with $V$ in place of $W_0$, either every $f \in B$ lies in $F_0$ with the resulting element in $V$, or there is $O \in$ `nodes` with $O \subseteq V$ and with every non-unit of $O$ lying in the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   Finally, every $O \in$ `nodes` satisfies: $O \subseteq W_0$; $O$ is a local Noetherian ring; $O \cap k_0 = A \cap k_0$ (for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $O$); every $f \in O$ is congruent to a constant, in the sense that there is $x \in k_0 \cap A$ with image in $O$ such that $f - x$ is not a unit of $O$; and there exist a natural number $E_0 \ge 1$, a unit $v$ of $A \cap k_0$ (an element $v$ of $k_0$ with $v, v^{-1} \in A$) with $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,2\,w} v$, where $w =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, a proof that the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $O$, elements $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` of the adic completion $\hat A_0$ of $A \cap k_0$ at its maximal ideal with parameter the image of $\pi_0^{E_0}$, that is $\hat A_0[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - \pi_0^{E_0})$, and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that crossing model, such that:
--
--   $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$ in $O$; $\iota$ sends the image of every $x \in k_0 \cap A$ whose image lies in $O$ to `UVCrossingModel.const` of the image of $x$ in $\hat A_0$; $\iota$ sends $c_x$ to $\gamma_U \cdot$ `UVCrossingModel.U` and $c_y$ to $\gamma_V \cdot$ `UVCrossingModel.V`, the two distinguished elements of the crossing model; $c_y$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, whereas $c_x$, whenever it lies in $W_0$, is not in the maximal ideal of $W_0$;
--
--   there exists a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ with $O \subseteq W_x$, with $W_x \cap k_0 = A \cap k_0$, which is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$, which contains an element $t$ with the property that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ then every coefficient of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$; such that $c_x$, whenever in $W_x$, lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$, and $c_y$, whenever in $W_x$, does not; and such that for every $g \in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose image lies in `R₀.integers` and which has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ at which $j_q$ has non-negative order, the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_x$, it lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ if and only if the $R_0$-residue of $g$ is zero, and if that residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$ then the image of $g$ lies in $O$ and, for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose image lies in $O$ and whose residue in the residue field of $A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of the image of $g$ and of $c$ is not a unit of $O$;
--
--   and there exists a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ such that every $f \in B_x$ has image in $B$ and lies in $O$; every $f \in B_x$ has non-negative order at every place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ at which the image of $j_q$ has non-negative order; $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ at its non-units, in the sense that $f \in O$ if and only if $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in B_x$ with $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h \in O$; $F_0$ is the fraction field of $B_x$, every $f \in F_0$ being of the form $g/h$ with $g, h \in B_x$, $h \ne 0$; and $B_x$ is of finite type over the constants, being the subring generated by the set of images of elements of $k_0 \cap A$ together with a finite set $T$ of elements of $F_0$.
--
--   This is the construction, over a prescribed level field $F_0$ (the elements of the full $q^2M'$-level function field whose $q$-expansion coefficients lie in the small constant field $k_0$), of the affine chart of the descended model of the modular curve at a supersingular point of the level-$M'$ curve, of the discrete valuation ring lying over that supersingular place, and of the $q+1$ nodes of the fibre, whose completed local rings are given by the crossing model $\hat A_0[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\pi_0^{E_0})$, with the special fibre of the chart identified with the Drinfeld curve of level $q$. It has the same hypotheses as [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_of_levelField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_of_levelField) and retains part of that theorem's conclusion; it is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_drinfeldRing_iff_localization_formallySmooth_card_le_descent`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_drinfeldRing_iff_localization_formallySmooth_card_le_descent) and by the chart-only form [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_of_levelField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_of_levelField).
